SEL: with ``sel.attempt_more_commands``, PEAT also runs ``HELP``, ``CAS``, ``VER``, ``TIM Q``, ``GOO``, ``STA A`` (400 series), ``SNS``, ``DNA X``, ``BNA``, ``CST``, and ``SHO`` (``sel.show_settings``) over Telnet and serial, in the same order on both, and parses the output into the data model (e.g. the time source, GOOSE peers in ``related.hosts``, self-test results, and the settings from ``SHO`` if no settings file was downloaded). The output of each command is saved and hashed in ``ascii_commands/``.
